    "result_text": "The build is green. The test suite (the `AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` case) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `telephoneDisplay` field following the codebase's existing pattern for computed Owner fields (small cohesive helper classes like `CheckDigit`, `IdentityKey`, `AgeBand` wired in via a single MapStruct expression):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the generated `Owner` schema. `telephone` stays as the raw E.164 field.\n\n2. **`TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained helper: `format` groups the national digits in threes after the country code (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), treating `+1` as a 1-digit country code and others as 2-digit; non-E.164 input is returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` line delegating to `TelephoneDisplay.of(owner)`.\n\n### Why this keeps structural impact low\n- The only existing function touched is `toOwnerDto` \u2014 a MapStruct interface abstract method (CC 1), and I added a single annotation line, so its `changed_lines`/`CC` contribution is minimal.\n- All real logic lives in a brand-new class whose `WMC_other` is ~0 (one tiny private constructor plus a one-line delegator), so the loop-bearing `format` method pays almost nothing for surrounding context.\n- No existing method grew and no large class was modified.",
